<LessonLayout title="Catechist's Guide &mdash; The Passions and Moral Conscience" cic="CCC 1762-1802" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For preparing and leading the class.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated time:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Core topic:</strong> The passions (emotions) are a gift from God that must be ordered by reason enlightened by faith, and conscience is the inner voice that guides us to distinguish good from evil.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that passions are not evil in themselves; their morality depends on how we use them.</li>
<li>Understand what moral conscience is and why it must be formed.</li>
<li>Distinguish between certain, doubtful, and erroneous conscience.</li>
<li>Recognize how passions can cloud or help the judgment of conscience.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> &laquo;Blessed are the pure in heart, for they shall see God&raquo; (Mt 5:8)</p>
<p><strong>Catechism references:</strong> CCC 1762-1802</p>

</section>

